/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (       Over the years, some pranks have become especially memorable, standing out for their creativity or humor. Ms. Fitzgerald recalls examples such as hundreds of carefully placed cups covering the entire lobby of Wilkie, forcing anyone who entered to navigate the space slowly and carefully to avoid spilling them. She also remembers students saran wrapping faculty cars, turning an ordinary parking lot into a scene of confusion and laughter. These pranks exemplify the creativity and humor that define the tradition. The most successful pranks are the ones that surprise the community while remaining harmless. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [44]
>>
